WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.624
Let's summarize Module 2 A strong relational table
has a clear

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.223
subject and a clear row grain Keys solve different
problems Primary

00:00:12.249 --> 00:00:16.684
and surrogate keys provide stable row identity
natural and alternate keys protect

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:22.578
business identifiers composite keys identify
combinations and foreign keys connect related tables

00:00:24.331 --> 00:00:28.054
Cardinality tells us where foreign keys belong and
when a junction table

00:00:28.081 --> 00:00:33.791
is needed Constraints turn important business rules
into database-enforced

00:00:33.817 --> 00:00:39.897
guardrails Normalization reduces repeated facts and
update insertion

00:00:40.081 --> 00:00:45.618
and deletion anomalies Finally good operational
design creates

00:00:45.631 --> 00:00:51.254
a more trustworthy source for analytical models The
coding habit to carry

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.701
forward is simple run a correct example change one
part complete one

00:00:55.728 --> 00:01:00.217
rule and then write a small version yourself Module
3 builds on

00:01:00.243 --> 00:01:03.164
this foundation with querying and controlled data
changes
